    "changelog": [
      "When to Segment: added guidance to preserve quoted terms until their explanatory head appears, to delay committing temporal modifiers until their modified head is visible, and to avoid forcing name/parenthetical finalization prematurely — implements the critic's 'wait-for-head' and quoted-gloss rules.",
      "Never Segment: added an explicit prohibition on inserting a boundary inside a compound agent/occupation word (e.g. splitting before or inside ...员) because that always produces unrenderable fragments.",
      "Priority Rules: merged the candidate_rules into the ranking hierarchy: demote/don't finalize boundaries that would force premature transliteration/translation of names or parentheticals, delay boundaries after possessive 的 or modifier phrases until the head noun, avoid finalizing temporal modifiers or century phrases before the head, keep modifier+head (including coordinated heads) together, treat named-entity/species ambiguity as a signal to preserve source form or rank the boundary low, and explicitly lower ranks for comma-adjacent candidates when the following tokens start a modifier, parenthesis, quote, possessive 的, date/number, or a compound head."
    ],
    "next_changelog": [
      "[When to Segment]: Clarified that positions which end on modifiers (e.g. 的), numerals+century, open quotes after 意思是, parenthetical/parenthesis openings, organisation names immediately followed by an acronym, and other incomplete-head signals should be marked as candidates but treated as risky until the head or closing token appears — this reduces premature lexical commitment while preserving candidates.",
      "[Never Segment]: Removed any added blanket ban on splitting inside compound agent/occupation words; kept only absolute, corpus-wide forbids (punctuation attachment, breaking dates/numerals, cutting mid-parenthetical/quote, start/end). This relaxes an over-broad prohibition that previously prevented useful candidates.",
      "[Priority Rules]: Added explicit ranking guidance to demote (but not forbid) boundaries that would finalize entity lexicalisations, titles/roles, dates/temporal modifiers, or NP heads when such items are likely completed by following tokens; promote boundaries only after main predicates, head nouns, or closing quote/parenthesis appear.",
      "[Decision Procedure]: Added a lightweight post-ranking re-evaluation pass that detects candidates that terminate in open modifiers (的), open quotes/parentheses, numerals+世纪/date fragments, reporting/compliment- expecting verbs, or unstable prepositional/comparative prefixes and pushes them to the bottom of the ranking rather than removing them."
    ]
